Subject: [PATCH 7/7] sdcardfs: backport from LineageOS kenzo, with its VFS hooks

Pie's sdcard daemon has no FUSE path any more. system/core/sdcard/sdcard.cpp
in LineageOS 16.0 mounts sdcardfs (or esdfs) and nothing else; when the mount
fails it aborts with "failed to sdcardfs_setup", vold gives up on the emulated
volume, and /storage stays an empty tmpfs: no /sdcard for any app. Setting
persist.sys.sdcardfs=force_off does not help -- it only picks esdfs instead.
This kernel has neither.

Same source as patch 0004, for the same reasons: LineageOS' kernel for the
Xiaomi Redmi Note 3 Pro (kenzo, android_kernel_xiaomi_msm8956, lineage-15.0),
the same SoC and the same Qualcomm CAF 3.10 base. Its sdcardfs starts with
"sdcardfs: port to 3.10", so it was written for this kernel version.

The series is every kenzo commit that touches fs/sdcardfs, plus the ones
outside it that sdcardfs needs, found by commit message and by comparing the
result with kenzo's files (each one below is Android's, or an upstream
backport the next one builds on):

  d_canonical_path, so inotify on an sdcardfs path watches the lower file;
  private mount data, permission2, setattr2 and truncate2, for sdcardfs'
  per-mount views (/mnt/runtime/{default,read,write});
  remount propagation to slaves of slaves, and the two propagate_mnt
  backports it sits on;
  the change of SDCARDFS_SUPER_MAGIC, which touches only magic.h.

