The result is identical to kenzo's in fs/sdcardfs/, magic.h, mount.h and
pnode.[ch]. The other files differ from kenzo only by changes kenzo has and
sdcardfs does not need: file-based encryption (fscrypt), LineageOS' su
hooks, and three security fixes (coredump O_EXCL, path_connected for
CVE-2015-2925, check_mnt in collect_mounts). Those are worth taking
separately; they are not part of this.

The defconfig sets CONFIG_SDCARD_FS=y (CONFIGFS_FS, which it depends on, was
already on).
